  "final_text": "The `android.os.NetworkOnMainThreadException` was caused by performing network I/O synchronously on the main thread when `load.setOnClickListener` invoked `CatalogClient().fetchCatalog()`.\n\n### Changes Made\n\nIn [MainActivity.kt](file:///mnt/01DC198BE9192500/github/Schooldev/3S-study-work/trials/e4/c3-agy-A-r1/work/app/src/main/kotlin/vn/shelftap/lab/MainActivity.kt#L25-L36):\n- Used `lifecycleScope.launch` to launch a coroutine attached to the activity lifecycle.\n- Wrapped the blocking call `CatalogClient().fetchCatalog()` in `withContext(Dispatchers.IO)` so network requests execute on an I/O background thread.\n- The response (or exception message) is returned and assigned to `output.text` back on the main thread.\n",
